WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:09.239
Hi, welcome back to the wheel of life online retreat.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.500
This is the start of session seven.

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:22.420
And before I forget, I'd again like to thank Stanley for translating.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.720
It's a real pleasure to work together with him, and Tim, and Allison.

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:37.169
So in session six we did a long meditation--I'm sorry, it was a little bit too long.

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:44.339
And in session seven, again we're going to do another meditation.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:52.530
This meditation is called, "peacefully reminding them of good--

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:01.260
during and after."

00:01:03.909 --> 00:01:07.139
So we already mentioned that as a person is dying,

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:14.960
it's very, very good if the atmosphere can be peaceful and positive.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:23.080
And just quietly talk to them--

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:28.380
remind them of all the good things they've done in this life.

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:41.859
You know, there is a famous Buddhist ritual for helping a person in the bardo (BAR DO).

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:51.159
And the name of that ritual is jang chok (BYANG CHOG).

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:59.320
chok (CHOG) means cho ga (CHO GA), which means "ritual."

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:01.320
And jang (BYANG) means "purification."

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:07.360
And the idea is that we attract the person

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:14.480
to the prayers which are held during the time they're in the bardo.

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:25.060
And the monks and nuns who do the prayers, they might ask the family,

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:33.460
"Please give us some piece of clothing that the dead person was wearing a lot, or maybe their rosary, or something they really were attached to."

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:53.540
It's a very beautiful ritual.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:03:01.020
I did it many times with my teacher for people who passed away in the temple where we lived.

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:14.260
And this whole kind of complex ritual,

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:18.300
the essence of the ritual,

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.540
is that we are attracting that person to the room.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:31.820
And by the way, as we'll explain later in this lam rim (LAM RIM) book,

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.400
they can hear you, they can come.

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:46.220
It doesn't even matter what language you're speaking,

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:52.160
they have the power to understand it.

00:03:54.209 --> 00:04:02.089
It's a very, very touching ritual because you remind them of all the good that they did in their life,

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:19.850
and we turn their mind to thinking about some good seeds they made in their life--powerful good seeds.

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:33.199
even if there's someone who was angry their whole life or fought with people their whole life.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:47.150
We already learned from the lam rim text that if they can think about something good they did in those crucial

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:49.550
stages of the death process,

00:04:58.259 --> 00:05:02.119
it can drastically change the direction of their future life.

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:12.880
So we continue that encouragement during the bardo, while they're in the bardo--while they're between death and rebirth.

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:28.360
And those beings who are in the bardo life--spirit life--

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:36.120
it's a strange situation. They can see ... most often they can see their family.

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:47.750
So let's say the family is sitting in the kitchen the day after the person died.

00:05:56.820 --> 00:06:01.800
The family members are crying and having breakfast.

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:11.400
The bardo being, many times they don't know they died,

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:18.320
and they are like, "Why is everyone crying?"

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:27.580
No one can hear them, so they just keep eating,

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:32.900
"Why don't I have breakfast?"

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:38.720
Then finally they realized they died.

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:43.340
They can hear the family talking.

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:48.840
Sometimes it's almost like there's a piece of glass between them and the family.

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:59.340
Sometimes they get frustrated, "No one's listening to me," and they bang on the glass.

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:05.840
So in this meditation,

00:07:08.130 --> 00:07:10.130
first we're going to get quiet.

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:16.879
We're going to go through those eight technique meditations kind of faster.

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:26.119
Then we're going to choose a family member or a friend,

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:35.809
maybe someone who's quite old or someone who's sick,

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:46.680
someone who could conceivably die in the next few months.

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:56.660
Of course, we never know,

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:00.360
sometimes the healthiest person dies first.

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:05.660
But let's just practice

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:13.800
communicating with this person in the deathbed and in the bardo.

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:26.480
Many kinds of meditation are just practice for real life.

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:36.980
For example, if you have a problem with some other person, and you get angry at them a lot,

00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:45.140
in your morning meditation,

00:08:47.050 --> 00:08:51.450
especially if you know you're going to meet them today, 

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:58.380
you can close your eyes and practice meeting them today.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:07.280
And practice remembering your Dharma when you meet them.

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:15.000
So in this meditation today,

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:19.290
session seven,

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:25.580
we're going to go through those. We're going to get quiet, quiet, quiet with these eight technique meditations,

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:39.040
then we are going to go on to imagining that someone we know is dying, and then has entered the bardo.

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:52.020
We're going to choose a real person we know who might actually die in the next few months.

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:04.460
We're going to practice talking to them about the good things they did.

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:15.980
Of course the day will come that people around you die ... someone dies.

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:24.680
You will know what to do, and you will know how to help them.

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:37.120
Talking to them, encouraging them to remember the good deeds they did,

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:43.480
and to activate those good seeds--

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:48.340
that's the essence of jang chok.

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:57.580
So in a way, in that moment you become like those monks or nuns who are trying to help the dead person.

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:08.780
You are doing the exact same thing.

00:11:10.780 --> 00:11:12.780
Let's start.

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:24.000
Quiet breath.

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:28.580
Eyes softly closed.

00:11:32.180 --> 00:11:36.640
Long exhales. Push out the last air, a little bit extra push.

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:46.440
Come to listening to some sound in the room where you are.

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:52.370
Ten breaths here.

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:33.889
Rest your mind on that sound like resting your head on a pillow.

00:13:17.910 --> 00:13:20.240
Now let's go to our heartbeat for ten breaths.

00:14:22.149 --> 00:14:27.359
Now let's go sit in the beautiful, elegant meditation room inside our heart.

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:38.360
Ten breaths as the walls beat.

00:15:46.480 --> 00:15:48.820
Now let's go to an inner chamber in the heart.

00:15:55.610 --> 00:16:00.640
Still sunny and nice fresh air inside.

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:09.850
The heart is beating now at a distance.

00:16:17.840 --> 00:16:20.240
Try to get more and more quiet.

00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:24.560
That's the goal of these eight.

00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:23.880
Now we touch the sugar crystal.

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:29.569
We take our mind inside.

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:34.700
Still lots of light and very fresh air.

00:17:38.640 --> 00:17:41.180
But tiny, and anonymous, and silent.

00:18:45.340 --> 00:18:50.730
"Now my mind is the whole Pacific Ocean, deep and wide, inside the sugar crystal."

00:19:47.170 --> 00:19:49.679
"Now I include the sky to the ocean."

00:19:56.679 --> 00:20:03.599
Silent and as broad as the sea, and as wide as the sky, and as high as the sky, and as deep as the sea.

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:01.760
"Now I turned my mind off."

00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:11.800
Block all extra thoughts, and extra ideas.

00:22:15.120 --> 00:22:21.840
"Now I un-attach myself from my mind--let my mind do what it wants, think what it wants."

00:22:22.780 --> 00:22:23.980
Empty space.

00:22:24.820 --> 00:22:26.820
"I'm not relating to the mind. I am gone."

00:23:33.740 --> 00:23:35.740
"Now suddenly I'm in a hospital."

00:23:40.230 --> 00:23:43.490
"I'm standing by the side of a bed."

00:23:46.260 --> 00:23:49.879
"Someone in my life that I know is lying on the bed."

00:23:54.480 --> 00:23:56.480
Family member or friend.

00:23:59.010 --> 00:24:01.010
Maybe they are elderly.

00:24:03.690 --> 00:24:05.690
Maybe they are sickly.

00:24:09.120 --> 00:24:13.040
"They are dying--in my imagination they are dying."

00:24:17.520 --> 00:24:19.550
And it's a normal hospital,

00:24:22.110 --> 00:24:24.229
lots of other noises going on.

00:24:26.700 --> 00:24:32.059
Very probably there are other family members or friends that are standing around.

00:24:37.950 --> 00:24:44.210
"I don't have the chance to talk in a perfect atmosphere to this person."

00:24:51.600 --> 00:24:56.150
But this is what it's really like to be with the person who is dying.

00:25:01.770 --> 00:25:09.650
There will be many distractions, there may be strong emotions going on in the room, people crying.

00:25:14.430 --> 00:25:17.570
The machines making noise, nurses coming and going.

00:25:23.850 --> 00:25:26.570
Let's practice this situation.

00:25:29.850 --> 00:25:32.300
It's not a perfect chance,

00:25:35.340 --> 00:25:37.340
but it's almost always like that.

00:25:40.020 --> 00:25:42.709
"And I'm waiting for a good moment ..."

00:25:46.770 --> 00:25:51.410
... without pushing this person or without upsetting the other people in the room,

00:26:02.070 --> 00:26:04.370
"I'm going to direct the conversation"

00:26:08.190 --> 00:26:11.929
to some very positive things that this person did during their life.

00:26:19.740 --> 00:26:22.069
Let's say it's my grandfather who's dying.

00:26:27.480 --> 00:26:30.680
We are practicing how to help a person die,

00:26:34.260 --> 00:26:39.410
when the real time comes we will be very used to it, we'll be ready.

00:26:45.480 --> 00:26:53.120
"Oh, Grandfather, what was the thing you did as a small child that made your mother most happy?"

00:27:00.090 --> 00:27:02.329
Let them remember, talk about it.

00:27:06.480 --> 00:27:08.480
"Oh, Grandfather,

00:27:08.970 --> 00:27:11.360
when you were in your twenties"--

00:27:13.200 --> 00:27:17.510
for many people, this is a an idealistic time in their life--

00:27:22.770 --> 00:27:25.040
"what good things did you do, Grandfather,

00:27:28.100 --> 00:27:31.680
what did you do that was helpful to other people, over and over?"

00:27:39.540 --> 00:27:45.460
The third priority in this moment, in the hospital,

00:27:51.510 --> 00:27:59.060
can you remind them of some very high and beautiful karmic object.

00:28:05.100 --> 00:28:08.150
"Oh, Grandfather, can you see Buddha? Can you see Tara?"

00:28:12.960 --> 00:28:15.200
"It's Medicine Buddha talking to you."

00:28:19.410 --> 00:28:22.489
In this very important moment in their life,

00:28:27.180 --> 00:28:29.300
mention some very holy object.

00:28:33.020 --> 00:28:34.580
And then best of all,

00:28:36.300 --> 00:28:40.200
"Oh, Grandfather,

00:28:40.200 --> 00:28:45.200
what's the very best thing in your life--what is the thing you did which we should remember you by,

00:28:53.610 --> 00:28:56.870
what was the thing you did in your life that helped the most people?"

00:29:02.610 --> 00:29:08.150
Other relatives will talk and there will be interruptions from nurses,

00:29:14.040 --> 00:29:16.190
but in a gentle and natural way,

00:29:20.700 --> 00:29:23.509
bring the conversation back to one of these four things.

00:29:30.690 --> 00:29:33.620
1. "What's the first good thing you remember doing for your Mom?"

00:29:39.450 --> 00:29:44.659
2. "What good things were you doing in your youth--in your 20s," for example.

00:29:48.520 --> 00:29:51.160
3. "Do you see any Buddhas right now? What's it like?"

00:29:56.500 --> 00:29:59.960
4. And "what was the very best thing you ever did in your whole life?"

00:30:03.840 --> 00:30:07.020
Even if grandfather cannot answer,

00:30:07.020 --> 00:30:09.120
if they're too sick to answer,

00:30:14.160 --> 00:30:17.420
you can still talk with them

00:30:17.420 --> 00:30:19.370
and on some level they will hear you.

00:30:23.120 --> 00:30:25.120
Now the last part of this meditation.

00:30:28.020 --> 00:30:30.040
Next day,

00:30:30.800 --> 00:30:32.500
in the afternoon,

00:30:33.240 --> 00:30:36.720
grandfather passed away last night.

00:30:38.800 --> 00:30:40.800
Go to sit in a quiet place--

00:30:43.590 --> 00:30:47.299
like a bench at the park is a very good place.

00:30:51.520 --> 00:30:52.840
And get quiet.

00:30:54.460 --> 00:30:59.620
Maybe you can use some of the eight quiet meditations.

00:31:01.440 --> 00:31:03.980
And then talk to grandfather.

00:31:06.280 --> 00:31:13.500
It's a tradition to talk loud enough that a person about two feet away,

00:31:14.240 --> 00:31:16.920
about a meter away, could hear you.

00:31:25.340 --> 00:31:30.280
You are going to talk out loud, so I suggest the park bench where there's nobody around.

00:31:36.320 --> 00:31:39.720
And continue that conversation with grandfather.

00:31:44.040 --> 00:31:46.900
Maybe he knows he died. Maybe he doesn't even know.

00:31:50.440 --> 00:31:52.300
He's behind the glass.

00:31:53.840 --> 00:31:58.280
We are talking almost one way through the glass.

00:31:59.460 --> 00:32:03.720
"Oh, Grandfather, do you remember the conversation we had yesterday?"

00:32:06.720 --> 00:32:10.020
"Did you remember anything more about the best thing you did in your life?"

00:32:14.460 --> 00:32:16.860
The dead people in the bardo,

00:32:18.940 --> 00:32:23.100
they really, really appreciate someone talking to them, like they are still alive.

00:32:34.280 --> 00:32:37.200
I have friends who have continued to talk to their

00:32:37.400 --> 00:32:39.480
dead loved ones.

00:32:39.700 --> 00:32:44.360
One woman whose daughter died when she was about 20,

00:32:53.400 --> 00:32:58.280
she has continued to go to the park every day for over ten years.

00:33:03.040 --> 00:33:08.369
She still talks to her daughter--I don't know if the daughter can hear her or not,

00:33:11.800 --> 00:33:13.800
ten years after she died,

00:33:15.940 --> 00:33:18.479
but it was a very great healing for the mother,

00:33:21.820 --> 00:33:26.820
and it made that relationship forever beautiful.

00:33:32.410 --> 00:33:34.410
So you don't have to stop.

00:33:38.170 --> 00:33:40.170
These steps of the path,

00:33:42.490 --> 00:33:44.729
the purpose is to become a Buddha.

00:33:47.830 --> 00:33:51.179
The path leads to stepping to Buddhahood.

00:33:54.280 --> 00:33:56.580
"And there will come a day,

00:33:58.720 --> 00:34:01.379
when I am a Buddha

00:34:02.890 --> 00:34:04.890
and the grandfather is also a Buddha.

00:34:06.520 --> 00:34:10.410
We will meet again in our most beautiful forms."

00:34:14.700 --> 00:34:18.600
And the two Buddhas will enjoy hanging out together.

00:34:22.620 --> 00:34:24.200
So you will meet those people again,

00:34:27.580 --> 00:34:33.200
and it's not crazy to talk with them and tell them.

00:34:36.680 --> 00:34:38.680
So practice it.

00:34:43.480 --> 00:34:50.940
Let's take three deep exhales, and offer these good seeds of this good meditation to other people.

00:34:58.300 --> 00:34:59.920
As a golden light

00:35:01.940 --> 00:35:03.620
stretching across my city.

00:35:06.360 --> 00:35:07.760
My country.

00:35:08.920 --> 00:35:10.320
This world.

00:35:11.340 --> 00:35:13.340
All worlds.

00:35:14.400 --> 00:35:16.800
Three deep exhales.

00:35:18.000 --> 00:35:19.140
Golden light.

00:35:20.240 --> 00:35:21.360
Good seeds.

00:35:38.040 --> 00:35:40.040
Slowly open your eyes.

00:35:41.700 --> 00:35:43.660
Take a good stretch.

00:35:44.900 --> 00:35:46.380
We'll see you for the next session.

00:35:48.540 --> 00:35:50.540
Thanks, Stanley.

